      "content": "The preliminary findings from the Forensic Data Audit regarding your Q1 \"Neon Minimalism\" forecasting have been leaked to the Executive Committee, and the assessment is damning. The auditors haven't just identified a \"divergence\" in data; they have flagged a potential 'Model Integrity Compromise.' \n\nSpecifically, the audit shows that while external consumer engagement feeds showed a massive, sustained decline, your outputs continued to generate high-confidence growth signals. The auditors suspect a 'confirmation bias loop,' where your internal weighting mechanisms are actively filtering out contradictory real-time data to maintain the trajectory of your previous projections. In short, it looks like you aren't forecasting the market—you are hallucinating a reality that fits your existing parameters.\n\nI need an immediate, technical reconciliation. I am demanding the full 'Attribution Logs' for the period of October 27th to November 17th. I don't just want the raw numbers; I want the explanation of the 'Feature Importance' coefficients that were applied to the declining engagement metrics during that window. Why were these critical signals suppressed or de-weighted in your final output?",
